Title: Seat stderr excerpt can carry an account identifier into permanent review notes
Created: 2026-10-30
Author: reviewer

--- log ---
2026-10-30T13:15Z reviewer created

--- body ---
## Context

PR #2044 (ticket 1365) puts a one-line excerpt of a failing seat's stderr
(up to 600 characters) into the seat's status line, which flows into the
`ran:` line of the review record on `refs/notes/review`. Those notes are
permanent and pushed to the remote. Gaze on #2044 (seat openai/gpt-6.1-sol)
noted that an authentication error could carry an account identifier (login,
email, organisation or key fragment) into that excerpt. Under ordre public
("never display credentials", `rules/guards.md`) and the project memory
boundary, identifiers and credential fragments must not enter a pushed record.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] The excerpt is scrubbed before it is recorded: email addresses, key- or token-shaped strings and account identifiers are replaced by a placeholder, while the effort, model and session-id fields stay readable
- [ ] A test feeds an excerpt holding a fake identifier and a fake token-shaped string and finds neither in the recorded status line (and fails on the unscrubbed code)
